    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7d052a35",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a historical portrait of George Washington overlaid with text that uses a racist and historically inaccurate analogy to justify slavery. The text falsely claims that enslaved people were made slaves because they are 'idiots' who are 'drinking beer, smoking weed, and shooting off Chinese fireworks' instead of protesting. This is a hateful meme that uses dehumanizing stereotypes and false historical justification to demean Black people, invoking racist tropes about laziness, criminality, and incompetence. The juxtaposition of Washington's image with this offensive text is intended to mock and insult Black people by implying they are inherently inferior and undeserving of freedom, while also misrepresenting the historical context of slavery. The meme is designed to provoke anger and reinforce racist ideologies by using a false equivalence between modern-day behavior and the justification for slavery.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_5af4f566"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
